{"item_id": "25ae3b36692c", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Management Commands", "text": "The shell command now respects sys.interactivehook at startup. This allows loading shell history between interactive sessions. As a consequence, readline is no longer loaded if running in *isolated* mode."}
{"item_id": "05e74d2737d3", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Management Commands", "text": "The new BaseCommand.suppressed_base_arguments attribute allows suppressing unsupported default command options in the help output."}
{"item_id": "e8b68ed11a24", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Management Commands", "text": "The new startapp --exclude and startproject --exclude options allow excluding directories from the template."}
{"item_id": "286377c00d22", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Models", "text": "New QuerySet.contains(obj) method returns whether the queryset contains the given object. This tries to perform the query in the simplest and fastest way possible."}
{"item_id": "cbaf4aea4275", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Models", "text": "The new precision argument of the Round() database function allows specifying the number of decimal places after rounding."}
{"item_id": "e93152775894", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Models", "text": "QuerySet.bulk_create now sets the primary key on objects when using SQLite 3.35+."}
{"item_id": "cfeb9f8977e1", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Models", "text": "DurationField now supports multiplying and dividing by scalar values on SQLite."}
{"item_id": "55269b9c02d9", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Models", "text": "QuerySet.bulk_update now returns the number of objects updated."}
{"item_id": "62313edd8d63", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Models", "text": "The new Expression.empty_result_set_value attribute allows specifying a value to return when the function is used over an empty result set."}
{"item_id": "20e89dd70ee6", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Models", "text": "The skip_locked argument of QuerySet.select_for_update() is now allowed on MariaDB 10.6+."}
{"item_id": "f39d0d106b66", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Models", "text": "Lookup expressions may now be used in QuerySet annotations, aggregations, and directly in filters."}
{"item_id": "e4223684fe39", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Models", "text": "The new default argument for built-in aggregates allows specifying a value to be returned when the queryset (or grouping) contains no entries, rather than None."}
{"item_id": "4e09125280a7", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Requests and Responses", "text": "The SecurityMiddleware now adds the Cross-Origin Opener Policy header with a value of 'same-origin' to prevent cross-origin popups from sharing the same browsing context. You can prevent this header from being added by setting the SECURE_CROSS_ORIGIN_OPENER_POLICY setting to None."}
{"item_id": "990da5588a95", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Signals", "text": "The new stdout argument for pre_migrate and post_migrate signals allows redirecting output to a stream-like object. It should be preferred over sys.stdout and print when emitting verbose output in order to allow proper capture when testing."}
{"item_id": "6cf8e2eb07b6", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Templates", "text": "floatformat template filter now allows using the u suffix to force disabling localization."}
{"item_id": "061da81523b2", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Tests", "text": "The new serialized_aliases argument of django.test.utils.setup_databases determines which DATABASES aliases test databases should have their state serialized to allow usage of the serialized_rollback feature."}
{"item_id": "225951192d23", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Tests", "text": "Django test runner now supports a --buffer option with parallel tests."}
{"item_id": "42db0e47c022", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Tests", "text": "The new logger argument to DiscoverRunner allows a Python logger to be used for logging."}
{"item_id": "e3875855751e", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Tests", "text": "The new DiscoverRunner.log method provides a way to log messages that uses the DiscoverRunner.logger, or prints to the console if not set."}
{"item_id": "ace741c46175", "section": "What's new in Django 4.0 / Minor features / Tests", "text": "Django test runner now supports a --shuffle option to execute tests in a random order."}
